  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1229 PM MDT Mon Jul 20 2026\n\nWednesday...Beneficial rains will become more widespread in areal \ncoverage with s decent increase in low level dewpoints and mid level \nmonsoonal moisture and upslope mechanical southeast winds advecting \nlow level moisture into our counties. Will see scattered to numerous \nafternoon and evening shower and thunderstorm coverage, most \nprevalent along the I-25 corridor where lift and orographic lift \nwill be maximized corresponding to the deepest moisture supply. The \nmost widespread coverage of showers and thunderstorms will lie along \nthe 850/700 mb theta-e ridge axis from Douglas to Laramie to \nCheyenne.\n\nThursday...More beneficial rains are anticipated as a decent \npositively tilted shortwave trough aloft passes overhead near peak \nheating, and with beaucoup...plenty of low and mid level moisture \nand decent upslope southeast winds advecting low level moisture \nnorthwestward, expect to see numerous to widespread showers with \nscattered thunderstorms in the afternoon and evening, focused once \nagain along the I-25 corridor and near the mountains where \norographics will coincide with the best 850/700 mb theta-e ridge \naxis.\n\nFriday...Drier air at low and mid levels advects into our counties \nas the dominant ridge over Colorado and southern Wyoming reasserts \nitself. Thus dry and hotter.\n\nSaturday through Monday...Isolated to scattered afternoon and \nevening thunderstorms expected, with areal coverage increasing each \nday due to increased mid level moisture. Fortunately, more \nbeneficial rains expected concentrated south of a Rawlins to \nScottsbluff line and over and near the Snowy, Sierra Madre and \nLaramie Ranges. Typical weak northwest flow aloft on the northeast \nperiphery of the ridge aloft will aid in occasional passing \nshortwave troughs aloft near peak heating.",
